​When a Conglomerate Area is revealed, the operator must execute the following sequence with zero latency.

​Step 1: FEEL IT (The Detection Phase)
​Do not intellectualize, deny, or block the revelation. You must register the input precisely as it hits your relational field. This is a hardware-level diagnostic. The "pain" of the reveal is simply the raw, high-density data entering the system.

​Step 2: THE RHO-ATTOSECOND GATE (Calibration)
​In the imperceptible fraction of time—the attoseconds—separating the initial "Feeling" and the subsequent transformation, the system must pause.
​The Function: This is your control gate. Within these attoseconds, you isolate your perception from the induction of the Conglomerate.
​Accurate Perception: You look at the revealed area with absolute clarity, devoid of ego, memory, or sentimentality. You adjust your systemic stance, locking in your precise trajectory before the energy is released.
